      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In this report we describe the case of a patient with a significant coronary artery dissection following percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) in whom serial coronary arteriograms were obtained over a 6-week period. These demonstrated healing of the dissected vessel and correlated with abatement of the patient's angina."},
